==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
From {{inh|en|enm|divisible}}, from {{der|en|fro|-}}, from {{der|en|LL.|divisibilis}}, from the verb {{der|en|la|divido|}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|[dɪˈvɪzɪbəɫ]}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-divisible.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Capable of being [[divide]]d or split.
# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} Of an [[integer]], that, when [[divide]]d by another integer, leaves no [[remainder]].
#: ''12 is '''divisible''' by 3.''

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|disunitable}}
* {{l|en|splittable}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|all meanings}} {{l|en|indivisible}}, {{l|en|non-divisible}}
* {{sense|capable of being divided}} {{l|en|combinable}}, {{l|en|mergeable}}, {{l|en|unifiable}}

